            "By **time** the cycle has three phases - **pre-impact** (warning, alerting, evacuation: the phase in which lives are actually saved), **impact** (the event and the first hours, when survival depends on local people and prior preparation), and **post-impact** (rescue, relief, rehabilitation and reconstruction, running from days to years).",
            "By **activity** it has four stages that repeat continuously and overlap in practice: **mitigation, preparedness, response and recovery**. Draw them as a wheel with the impact at the top.",
