            "**Response or relief** covers impact to about four to six weeks - search and rescue, triage, emergency care, evacuation, relief camps with water, sanitation, food and shelter, surveillance and outbreak control, care of the dead and psychosocial support.",
            "**Recovery** is subdivided into **rehabilitation** (restoring services, temporary shelter, livelihoods, restarting schools and health services) and **reconstruction** (rebuilding to a higher standard - 'build back better'), and every recovery decision becomes the mitigation phase of the next cycle.",
