            "**Water, sanitation and disease prevention planning**: identify sources that will remain usable, plan chlorination to a **free residual chlorine of 0.5 mg/L**, pre-position tankers, plan temporary latrines at no more than 20 persons per latrine sited more than 30 metres from and downhill of any water source, plan solid waste and carcass disposal, and set up a **syndromic surveillance format** for diarrhoea, fever with rash, jaundice and acute respiratory infection to run from day one.",
            "**Protect the facility and the vulnerable**: raise the plinth and the drug store, sandbag the entrance, move records, vaccines and equipment above the flood line, keep duplicate copies (electronic and physical) of the antenatal, tuberculosis and antiretroviral registers, plan pre-term shifting of women near delivery to a facility that will not be cut off, arrange advance drug supply for chronic patients, and pre-position drugs beyond the villages that get isolated.",
            "**IEC to the community in the local language**: boil or chlorinate all drinking water, do not walk or drive through moving water, keep documents, money and drugs in a waterproof packet, know your shelter and route, keep a 72-hour household kit, and report fever, diarrhoea or snake bite early. Coordinate all of this in writing with the **DDMA, revenue, irrigation, police, block development officer, panchayat and NGOs**, and keep a **redundant communication plan** - mobile, landline, VHF or HAM radio, runner - because the network fails first.",
