            "**L1 - district level.** The disaster can be managed with the resources of the district. The **District Disaster Management Authority under the District Magistrate / Collector** (co-chaired by the elected head of the district local authority, with the Superintendent of Police and the Chief Medical Officer as ex officio members) leads; the state is kept informed and on standby. Example: localised flooding of a few villages, or a bus accident with fifteen casualties.",
