    "Write the WHO definition of health planning verbatim in the first line: the orderly process of defining community health problems, identifying unmet needs, surveying the resources to meet them, establishing priority goals that are realistic and feasible, and projecting administrative action to accomplish the purpose of the proposed programme.",
    "**POSDCORB** - Planning, Organising, Staffing, Directing, COordinating, Reporting, Budgeting (Gulick and Urwick, 1937). Expand every letter; the mark is for the expansion, not the mnemonic.",
    "Goal, objective, target: a goal is broad and distant, an objective is specific and measurable, a target is the objective with a number and a date. Say which is which before listing any of them.",
