        "SWOT analysis is a structured situational analysis in which an organisation or a programme, in relation to one clearly stated objective, lists its internal Strengths and Weaknesses against the external Opportunities and Threats in its environment, so that a strategy can be built that uses what it has and defends what it lacks.",
        "It originated as the SOFT analysis of Albert Humphrey and colleagues at the Stanford Research Institute in the 1960s, and in health it is used at the situation-analysis step of the planning cycle - for a District Health Action Plan, a facility annual plan, a readiness assessment before quality certification, or the appraisal of a new service.",
