      answer: 3,
      difficulty: "easy",
      explanation:
        "Strengths and weaknesses are internal - attributes of the facility itself, which it controls. Opportunities and threats are external - features of the environment, which it can only respond to. Competition from private nursing homes is external and unfavourable, and is therefore a threat; it is not a weakness, because the PHC did not create it. The corresponding internal weakness might be that the labour room lacks privacy or that JSY payments are delayed. The distinction is the commonest source of lost marks: drug shortage in my PHC is a weakness, delay in the state supply chain is a threat. Threats are handled through the ST (use strengths to blunt threats) and WT (minimise both) pairings of the TOWS matrix.",
