        "IEC - Information, Education and Communication - is a planned, multi-channel process that combines the giving of accurate information, the imparting of understanding and skill through education, and two-way communication with a defined audience, in order to increase knowledge, change attitudes, create demand for services and bring about and sustain a desired health behaviour.",
        "It is the communication strategy of a health programme rather than a single activity, with its own objectives, audience, budget, materials, trained communicators and evaluation plan; it has since evolved into Behaviour Change Communication (BCC) and Social and Behaviour Change Communication (SBCC), and every national programme under the National Health Mission carries an IEC/BCC component with a dedicated budget line.",
