            "**Definition (UNICEF):** social mobilisation is the process of bringing together all feasible and practical intersectoral social allies to raise people's awareness of and demand for a particular development programme, to assist in the delivery of resources and services, and to strengthen community participation for sustainability and self-reliance.",
            "It is a **broad-scale movement** to engage people's participation in achieving a specific development goal through their own effort, working simultaneously through many sectors and many kinds of partner rather than through the health department alone.",
            "**Distinguish from related terms:** **community mobilisation** is the same process applied within a single community; **advocacy** is directed upward at policy makers and resource holders to win commitment, policy and money; **social marketing** is directed at the individual consumer through the marketing mix; **IEC/BCC** is planned communication with a segmented audience. All four are complementary layers of one health promotion strategy.",
