            "**It creates demand, not just supply.** Services that exist but are not asked for remain unused; mobilisation converts a scheme into a felt need, and this is what distinguishes a programme that achieves coverage from one that only achieves availability.",
            "**It mobilises resources the health sector does not have** - volunteers, meeting space, transport, loudspeakers, school children, credibility, media time and CSR funds - and multiplies the effect of a limited government budget.",
