            "**The ILO International Classification of Radiographs of Pneumoconioses** codes small opacities by shape and size (rounded p, q, r; irregular s, t, u) and by profusion on a 12-point scale from 0/- to 3/+, large opacities as A, B or C, and pleural abnormalities separately, read against standard films by a trained reader - it is the basis of surveillance and of compensation claims.",
