          points: [
            "**Sex ratio (India):** number of females per 1000 males in the population. **Child sex ratio:** females per 1000 males aged 0-6 years. **Sex ratio at birth:** female live births per 1000 male live births.",
            "**Natural sex ratio at birth is about 950 females per 1000 males**; a persistently lower figure in a large population indicates sex selection.",
            "**Census trend:** overall sex ratio 972 (1901) to 927 (1991, the lowest) to 933 (2001) to **943 (2011)**; child sex ratio 976 (1961) to 964 (1971) to 962 (1981) to 945 (1991) to 927 (2001) to **918 (2011)**. Urban child sex ratio 905 against rural 923.",
            "**NFHS-5 (2019-21) sex ratio at birth 929**, improved from 919 in NFHS-4; the SRS three-year average for 2018-20 was about 907.",
            "**Extremes (2011 census):** highest overall sex ratio Kerala 1084 and Puducherry 1037; lowest Haryana 879 and Punjab 895. Worst child sex ratios: Haryana 834, Punjab 846, Jammu and Kashmir 862, Delhi 871.",
            "**Magnitude:** Amartya Sen's 100 million missing women worldwide (1990); the Economic Survey 2017-18 estimated about **63 million missing women** in India and 21 million 'unwanted' girls.",
          ],
