  pearls: [
    "The **single fact the 2000 Act is remembered for** is the uniform age of **18 years for both sexes**; the 1986 Act had used 16 for boys and 18 for girls. Age is reckoned on the **date of the offence**.",
    "**Two categories, two bodies, no crossover:** child in conflict with law goes to the **Juvenile Justice Board**, child in need of care and protection to the **Child Welfare Committee**. Write this sentence first in any JJ answer.",
    "**Board composition:** a Metropolitan or Judicial Magistrate First Class plus **two social workers, at least one a woman**. **Committee composition:** a Chairperson plus **four members, at least one a woman and one a child expert**. These exact numbers are the marks.",
    "**Never death, never life imprisonment without the possibility of release, never a police lock-up or jail, never a joint trial with an adult, never disclosure of identity** - the five absolute bars under the JJ Act.",
    "The 2015 Act's **preliminary assessment** for a 16 to 18-year-old accused of a heinous offence assesses **capacity, understanding of consequences and circumstances** - it is not a trial, and the Children's Court may still decide to try the child as a child.",
    "**POCSO Section 19 binds every person, and the doctor above all; Section 21 punishes silence with six months.** There is no exemption for family wishes, for a private clinic, or for the doctor who thinks the police will make things worse.",
    "**A girl child under POCSO must be examined by a woman doctor**, in the presence of a trusted adult, and **the examination may proceed without an FIR** - the doctor does not wait for the police, and no hospital may refuse free treatment to a victim of a sexual offence.",
    "**NPEW 2001 in one line:** goal - advancement, development and empowerment of women; the three-part structure - **objectives, policy prescriptions, operational strategies**; and the two phrases examiners look for, **de jure and de facto equality** and **mainstreaming a gender perspective in the development process**.",
    "The **draft National Policy for Women 2016 was never notified**; NPEW 2001 remains in force. Say this rather than pretending the 2016 draft is the current policy.",
    "**Maternity Benefit Act after 2017: 26 weeks for the first two children, 12 for the third, 12 for a commissioning or adopting mother, creche at 50 employees.** The commonest number asked from all of women's legislation.",
    "**Sexual harassment at work:** the **Internal Complaints Committee** is compulsory at **10 or more employees**, at least **half its members women**, chaired by a senior woman, with a complaint window of three months and an inquiry completed in 90 days.",
    "When a question names a **superseded Act** - as the 2000 JJ Act now is - **answer the Act as asked, then add the replacement as a clearly labelled update**. Substituting the 2015 Act silently loses the marks for the question that was set.",
  ],
