        "It is a complete code for two groups of children - the child in conflict with law and the child in need of care and protection - providing for their care, protection, treatment, development, rehabilitation and social reintegration through a child-friendly approach in which institutionalisation is the last resort. (Note: the Act was repealed and replaced by the Juvenile Justice Act, 2015, further amended in 2021; the changes are set out at the end of this answer.)",
