            "**Child in conflict with law:** a child alleged or found to have committed an offence who had not completed 18 years on the date of the offence - dealt with by the **Juvenile Justice Board**.",
            "**Child in need of care and protection:** a child without a home or means of subsistence, found begging or on the street, working in contravention of labour law, abandoned or ill-treated, abused or likely to be abused or sexually exploited, trafficked or likely to be trafficked, missing or run-away, terminally ill without support, or a victim of armed conflict or natural calamity - dealt with by the **Child Welfare Committee**.",
